 CODING RULES — ALWAYS FOLLOW
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  1.  ALL Python functions must have type hints and docstrings
  2.  ALL new routes must have corresponding pytest tests
  3.  ALL new tables must have RLS policies (no exceptions)
  4.  NEVER expose SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY to the frontend
  5.  NEVER commit .env files (always use .env.example)
  6.  ALWAYS use the service layer (CaseService, ChatService, etc.)
      — never call Supabase directly from route handlers
  7.  ALWAYS use BaseAgent._safe_run() in the supervisor
  8.  ALWAYS add a legal disclaimer to every DraftingAgent output
  9.  ALWAYS use the existing shadcn/ui components — never raw HTML
  10. ALWAYS run ruff format + ruff check before committing
  11. New migrations go in supabase/migrations/ with timestamp prefix
  12. Use Conventional Commits: feat:, fix:, docs:, test:, chore:
  13. Match existing patterns — services/, routes/, agents/ structure
  14. Every error must be caught and returned as a structured
      JSON response via the exception handlers in core/exceptions.py
  15. Chat history passed to agents is always the last 10 messages

